    <h2>Not Sure Which Page Fits?</h2>

    <p>If you serve more than one of these markets — and most contractors do — your website should have a real page for each one, not a single line buried on a "service areas" page. That's the whole game in local search: a homeowner in <a href="/locations/madison/">Madison</a> finds the contractor whose page says Madison, and a homeowner in <a href="/locations/athens/">Athens</a> finds the one whose page says Athens. Want to see how your business currently stacks up across the cities you serve? <a href="/articles/local-seo-for-contractors/">Our local SEO playbook for contractors</a> walks through the mechanics, or just reach out and I'll do a free snapshot.</p>

